Subject: [PATCH 07228/11362] [outer-loop] bp35 L9 mapping round 18: door-shaft
 descent route identified, pillar-eye blocker

Sixth round on bp35 L9 (final level), still honest null. Key findings:
- Resolved round 17's control: LEFT from fall-through landing is SAFE without
  doors; the door-then-LEFT death is caused by door-opening, not movement.
- Doors are REAL passages (corrects round 17): opening the leftmost door carves
  an air shaft down cols13-17 = the goal's own columns (goal at cols14-16).
- The door-shaft fall dies on a color-11 B0B pillar eye at cols14-16 row20,
  blocking the shaft ABOVE the goal (GAME_OVER overview).
- Color-12 toggle blocks exist in L9 (rows8-12 overview), never seen live before.
- Lower-region color-8 switches are functional (corrects round 16's "exhausted").
- Reframe: player confined to cols>=13 by a solid cols6-12 wall in every state;
  goal pocket only opens via a cols0-5 shaft on the far side. Problem is now
  "reach the goal past the wall"; leftmost-door shaft is the intended descent.

All 4 load-bearing claims re-verified 3x from fresh env.reset() (deterministic).
Frontier stays at level 8.

